+---
+id: task-003-long-stay-discount
+type: task
+title: "Long-stay discount"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Long-stay discount
+
+## Request
+
+We want to reward customers who stay longer. A rental of 3 days or more now costs 10% less than its full
+price. Quotes and bookings both show the reduced total.
+
+## Choices made for this request
+
+- "3 days or more" means a rental of 3 or more rented days (the period from `start` to `end` in whole days).
+  A 2-day rental is priced at full price.
+- The discount is 10% of the full price (`dailyPrice * days`). The discounted total is an integer number of
+  euro cents, rounded half up to the nearest cent (for example 4665 cents, a 10% discount of 4198.5, becomes
+  4199).
+  Integer arithmetic only, no floats.
+- `quote` and `book` return the reduced total in `total`. The `Quote` and `Booking` shapes do not change.
+- `availability` is unaffected: it reserves nothing and returns ids only.
+- Existing expectations for 3-day rentals in task-001 tests change to the reduced total; other tests are
+  unchanged.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC15: A rental of exactly 3 rented days is priced at 90% of the full price, in integer cents.
+- AC16: A rental of more than 3 days is priced at 90% of the full price (e.g. 10 days).
+- AC17: A rental of fewer than 3 days (1 or 2) is priced at the full price.
+- AC18: The discounted total is rounded half up to the nearest euro cent.
+- AC19: `book` returns the reduced total, the same as `quote` for the same request.
+- AC20: `book` still refuses an overlapping period, and a refused booking does not change state.
+
+## School rules (apply)
+
+1. Money is an integer number of euro cents.
+2. Times are UTC, written as ISO-8601 strings.
+3. A booking covers whole days: start and end are at midnight UTC.
+4. The same item cannot be booked for overlapping periods.
+
+## Traceability
+
+Feature: rental module (booking desk). Story: long stays are rewarded with a 10% discount.
+Requirements: school rules 1–4 above; changes the pricing of task-001 (AC2, AC5) and leaves task-002
+unchanged. Tests cover AC15–AC20 with happy and error paths.
